      "source": [
        "## 1. Dataset creation (synthetic, seed = 42)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why synthetic.** Public churn datasets (e.g. telecom or music-streaming churn data) lack FinSecure's wealth-management variables and, critically, a *future-revenue* column needed for a valid LTV target. A reproducible simulator is used instead.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Generative assumptions (all simulated):**\n",
        "* Three latent traits per customer – *engagement*, *frustration* and *payment stress* – drive the observable behaviour (logins, transactions, support tickets, late/failed payments).\n",
        "* **Churn label** = cancellation within the next **90 days**. Its probability is a logistic function of the observed behavioural features, tenure, promotion type, age group and independent noise (σ = 0.6), so the signal is imperfect by construction.\n",
        "* **Future-LTV target** = revenue actually generated over the **next 12 months** in USD = (months the customer stays in the 12-month window) × (effective monthly fee + monthly add-on revenue from investment activity) + noise. Customers who churn leave after 0.5–3 months; survivors face a small monthly hazard in months 4–12 that rises with their latent churn probability.\n",
        "* **Disclosed dependency:** the LTV target is built from the same latent churn event as the churn label, so the two targets are correlated *by construction*. The LTV regression models never receive the churn label as an input.\n",
        "* The USD 29 fee and promotional discounts (intro 30 %, loyalty 15 %, referral 10 %) follow the case brief. Add-on revenue = min(0.03 % × investment balance, USD 40) per month."
      ]
    },
