      "id": "e2a847c9",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e2a847c9"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Customer churn prediction\n",
        "**Protocol (no test leakage).**\n",
        "1. One stratified 80/20 train/test split (`random_state=42`). The test set is untouched until the single final evaluation.\n",
        "2. Preprocessing (median/most-frequent imputation, log transform for skewed amounts, standardisation, one-hot encoding) lives **inside** each `Pipeline`, so it is refit within every CV fold and on the training set only.\n",
        "3. Hyper-parameters are tuned by 5-fold stratified CV optimising **average precision** (PR-AUC), which is appropriate for an imbalanced positive (churn) class.\n",
        "4. **Model selection** uses cross-validated out-of-fold (OOF) average precision on the training data only.\n",
        "5. The **decision threshold** is chosen on OOF training predictions by maximising **F2** (recall weighted twice as heavily as precision), because missing a churner costs more than contacting a loyal customer.\n",
        "6. Class imbalance is addressed with `class_weight=\"balanced\"`; its effect is quantified against unweighted models on OOF data."
      ]
    },
