      "source": [
        "## 7. Integrating churn risk and LTV for retention prioritisation\n",
        "* **High-risk** = churn tier \"High\". **High-LTV** = predicted 12-month LTV ≥ the **median of actual LTV in the training set** (illustrative cut-off).\n",
        "* Each customer is assigned to one of four action groups.\n",
        "* **Hypothetical ROI scenario (NOT a measured outcome):** assumed cost per contacted customer = USD 12 and assumed save rate (uplift) *s*. \"Revenue at stake\" for a customer = 12 × current monthly revenue run-rate (historical revenue ÷ tenure). For a targeting rule, the *realised* revenue at stake is the sum over targeted customers who actually churned (synthetic labels); hypothetical benefit = *s* × that sum − cost × customers contacted. Whether an offer truly retains anyone must be tested in a randomised experiment."
      ]
    },
